 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -8,12 +8,13 @@\n def construct(n=13):\n     \"\"\"Return a list of n points (x, y) inside the closed unit square [0,1]^2.\n \n-    The score is the smallest area among all triangles with corners at three of\n-    the points, so no three points may be (nearly) collinear. This start puts\n-    the points on a regular polygon on a small circle around the center, which\n-    avoids collinear triples but wastes most of the square.\n+    The objective is to maximize the smallest area among all triangles with\n+    corners at three of the points, so no three points may be (nearly) collinear.\n+    This variant uses a larger circle radius to spread out points, which reduces\n+    the chance of small triangle areas and improves the number of triangles near\n+    the minimum.\n     \"\"\"\n-    radius = 0.3\n+    radius = 0.5  # The radius of the circle around the center (increased from 0.3)\n     return [(0.5 + radius * math.cos(2 * math.pi * k / n),\n              0.5 + radius * math.sin(2 * math.pi * k / n)) for k in range(n)]\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
